<h1>puressh apt repository</h1>
<p>
  A pure-Rust SSH suite, packaged for Ubuntu 20.04, 22.04 and 24.04
  (amd64 and arm64). Source and docs:
  <a href="https://github.com/KarpelesLab/puressh">github.com/KarpelesLab/puressh</a>.
</p>

<h2>Install</h2>
<pre><code>curl -fsSL @PAGES_URL@/puressh-archive-keyring.asc \
  | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/puressh.gpg
echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/puressh.gpg] @PAGES_URL@ $(lsb_release -cs) main" \
  | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/puressh.list
sudo apt update
sudo apt install puressh-server   # drop-in sshd replacement
# or: sudo apt install puressh-client   # ssh/scp/sftp/... alongside OpenSSH</code></pre>

<p>
  Installing <code>puressh-server</code> removes <code>openssh-server</code> but
  keeps <code>/etc/ssh/sshd_config</code> and the host keys. Switch back any time
  with <code>sudo apt install openssh-server</code>.
</p>

